01:02:22.220 --> 01:02:25.460
So that is that you have computed your open loop trajectory

01:02:25.460 --> 01:02:27.100
which corresponds to,

01:02:30.900 --> 01:02:32.100
which corresponds, sorry,

01:02:32.100 --> 01:02:35.540
I computed the open loop trajectory,

01:02:35.540 --> 01:02:39.660
which meaning the desired U,

01:02:39.660 --> 01:02:43.140
which translates into a desired X.

01:02:46.780 --> 01:02:48.500
Of course, X is related to U

01:02:48.500 --> 01:02:50.740
through the differential equation of motion.

01:02:50.740 --> 01:02:52.460
So this is the desired quantity

01:02:52.460 --> 01:02:57.460
that you would like your system to always track perfectly.

01:02:59.340 --> 01:03:03.260
In this control law, this XD will be here

01:03:03.260 --> 01:03:04.620
along with its derivatives.

01:03:06.340 --> 01:03:09.500
And the UD is the first term

01:03:09.500 --> 01:03:12.140
that you will have in the combined control law.

01:03:14.140 --> 01:03:17.820
So, and here the pi will be the non-linear transformation

01:03:17.820 --> 01:03:20.220
that allows you to go from the original system

01:03:20.220 --> 01:03:22.300
to the differential fact representation

01:03:22.980 --> 01:03:24.060
times the error terms.

01:03:26.060 --> 01:03:27.020
Does it make sense?

01:03:29.340 --> 01:03:32.980
So the procedure is very structured.

01:03:32.980 --> 01:03:35.180
You first compute the open loop trajectory.

01:03:35.180 --> 01:03:36.660
That becomes the desired one.

01:03:36.660 --> 01:03:38.500
Then you compute a tracking controller,

01:03:38.500 --> 01:03:42.260
which depends obviously on the desired trajectory,

01:03:42.260 --> 01:03:43.860
I mean, the open loop trajectory,

01:03:43.860 --> 01:03:46.100
because that's the one that you're trying to track.

01:03:48.220 --> 01:03:51.660
All right, last step, closed loop control.

01:03:51.740 --> 01:03:54.420
So this seems a bit of a touch.

01:03:54.420 --> 01:03:58.940
So as far as two-step design is concerned, we're done.

01:03:58.940 --> 01:04:00.460
But I still want to give you a little bit of intuition

01:04:00.460 --> 01:04:01.500
about closed loop control.

01:04:01.500 --> 01:04:03.460
Before doing so, there was a question.

